\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  Selection budget and ranking precision have distinct effects on candidate-restriction quality. At each $W$, restricted methods are compared with }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  Incremental-spread loss of PageRank pools relative to }\DIFaddendFL  the full reference \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  selected }\DIFdelendFL  at \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  that }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  the }\DIFaddendFL  same $W$\DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  , at the default ($\tau =10^{-6}$) and strict ($\tau =10^{-12}$) tolerance. Top row: 4k pools}\DIFaddendFL  ; \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  evaluation uses fixed independent worlds}\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  bottom row: 5\% pools}\DIFaddendFL  . Points are \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  mean incremental losses }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  means }\DIFaddendFL  over five \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  paired paths; }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  replicates and }\DIFaddendFL  bars are \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  path }\DIFdelendFL  standard deviations \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  . The plotted labels Default and Strict denote tolerances $10^{-6}$ and $10^{-12}$}\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  across replicates}\DIFaddendFL  ; \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  candidate membership is unchanged between $10^{-12}$ and $10^{-14}$. Negative }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  a positive }\DIFaddendFL  loss \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  favors }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  means that }\DIFaddendFL  the restricted set \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  reaches fewer vertices}\DIFaddendFL  . \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  The }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  On }\DIFaddendFL  ca-GrQc\DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  , the }\DIFaddendFL  default \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  reversal disappears with }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  PageRank-4k loss changes sign across budgets, whereas }\DIFaddendFL  the \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  tighter PageRank tolerance}\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  strict-tolerance loss stays below zero. On CollegeMsg and wiki-Vote}\DIFaddendFL  , \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  while }\DIFdelendFL  the \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  directed-network }\DIFdelendFL  losses persist \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  at both tolerances}\DIFaddendFL  .\DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  This is a post-hoc paired sensitivity analysis.}\DIFdelendFL  }}{13}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
