eginFL \DIFaddFL {strict-tolerance loss stays below zero. On CollegeMsg and wiki-Vote}\DIFaddendFL , \DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {while }\DIFdelendFL the \DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {directed-network }\DIFdelendFL losses persist \DIFaddbeginFL \DIFaddFL {at both tolerances}\DIFaddendFL .\DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {This is a post-hoc paired sensitivity analysis.}\DIFdelendFL }{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  Reference-set changes and independent spread changes, defined as higher-budget minus lower-budget }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  Change in }\DIFaddendFL  full-reference spread \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  . Filled circles denote changed final sets}\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  between two selection budgets (higher minus lower $W$) for each replicate on the SNAP networks: (a) $W=80$ to 320}\DIFaddendFL  ; \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  hollow squares denote unchanged sets. Paths }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  (b) $W=320$ to 1,280. Replicates }\DIFaddendFL  1101--1105 run from left to right within each graph. \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  Filled circles mark replicates whose final set changed, and hollow squares mark unchanged sets. }\DIFaddendFL  Bars are unadjusted 95\% \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  conditional }\DIFdelendFL  Monte Carlo intervals from 10,000 paired \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  evaluation }\DIFaddendFL  worlds. \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  Panel-specific vertical }\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  Vertical }\DIFaddendFL  scales \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red} \relax \fontsize  {7}{8}\selectfont  reveal small changes; the intervals condition on selected sets and do not describe variation across networks}\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue} \sf  differ between panels}\DIFaddendFL  .}}{14}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
